  "strategic_roadmap_for_round_5": {
    "core_thesis": "The Historical & Pedagogical Paradox of 'Tied Hands' in Poker Theory.",
    "key_arguments_to_deploy": [
      "1. Address Camp B's 'Three-Tier Trap' Claim directly: Camp B asserts Choice D is the 'intermediate trap'. But look at classic poker literature (Sklansky, Malmuth, Miller): when authors construct questions with 'Both X and Y', it is ALWAYS the correct answer testing equivalence at the strategic threshold, never a trick based on an unmentioned inside gutshot on rag runouts.",
